content:
You can choose between using CSS variables (recommended) or utility classes for theming.

<MermaidDiagram
  chart={`flowchart TD
  A[":root / .dark"] -->|"defines"| B["CSS Variables"]
  B --> C["--background / --foreground"]
  B --> D["--primary / --primary-foreground"]
  B --> E["--muted / --accent / --card"]
  B --> F["--destructive / --warning"]
  B --> G["--border / --input / --ring"]
  C -->|"mapped in @theme"| H["Tailwind Classes"]
  D -->|"mapped in @theme"| H
  E -->|"mapped in @theme"| H
  F -->|"mapped in @theme"| H
  G -->|"mapped in @theme"| H
  H --> I["bg-primary text-foreground border-border"]
`}
/>

## CSS Variables

```tsx /bg-background/ /text-foreground/
<div className="bg-background text-foreground" />
```

To use CSS variables for theming set `tailwind.cssVariables` to `true` in your `duck-ui.config.json` file.

```json {12} title="duck-ui.config.json" showLineNumbers
{
  "schema": "https://gentleduck.org/schema.json",
  "rsc": false,
  "monorepo": false,
  "workspace": {
    "root": ".",
    "project": "."
  },
  "tailwind": {
    "baseColor": "zinc",
    "css": "./src/styles/globals.css",
    "cssVariables": true,
    "prefix": ""
  },
  "aliases": {
    "ui": "~/ui",
    "libs": "~/libs",
    "hooks": "~/hooks",
    "pages": "~/pages",
    "layouts": "~/layouts"
  }
}
```

## Utility classes

```tsx /bg-zinc-950/ /text-zinc-50/ /dark:bg-white/ /dark:text-zinc-950/
<div className="bg-zinc-950 dark:bg-white" />
```

To use utility classes for theming set `tailwind.cssVariables` to `false` in your `duck-ui.config.json` file.

```json {12} title="duck-ui.config.json" showLineNumbers
{
  "schema": "https://gentleduck.org/schema.json",
  "rsc": false,
  "monorepo": false,
  "workspace": {
    "root": ".",
    "project": "."
  },
  "tailwind": {
    "baseColor": "zinc",
    "css": "./src/styles/globals.css",
    "cssVariables": false,
    "prefix": ""
  },
  "aliases": {
    "ui": "~/ui",
    "libs": "~/libs",
    "hooks": "~/hooks",
    "pages": "~/pages",
    "layouts": "~/layouts"
  }
}
```

## Convention

We use a simple `background` and `foreground` convention for colors. The `background` variable is used for the background color of the component and the `foreground` variable is used for the text color.

<Callout icon={<Lightbulb/>} title="Naming convention">
  The `background` suffix is omitted when the variable is used for the background color of the component. For example, `--primary` is the background and `--primary-foreground` is the text color.
</Callout>

Given the following CSS variables:

```css
--primary: oklch(0.205 0 0);
--primary-foreground: oklch(0.985 0 0);
```

The `background` color of the following component will be `var(--primary)` and the `foreground` color will be `var(--primary-foreground)`.

```tsx
<div className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground">Hello</div>
```

## List of variables

Here's the list of variables available for customization:

| Variable | Usage | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--background` | `bg-background` | Page background |
| `--foreground` | `text-foreground` | Default text color |
| `--primary` | `bg-primary` | Primary actions and emphasis |
| `--secondary` | `bg-secondary` | Secondary actions |
| `--muted` | `bg-muted` | Subtle backgrounds |
| `--accent` | `bg-accent` | Hover and active states |
| `--destructive` | `bg-destructive` | Error and danger actions |
| `--warning` | `bg-warning` | Warning states |
| `--card` | `bg-card` | Card backgrounds |
| `--popover` | `bg-popover` | Popover backgrounds |
| `--border` | `border-border` | Default borders |
| `--input` | `border-input` | Input borders |
| `--ring` | `ring-ring` | Focus rings |

```css title="app/globals.css" showLineNumbers
:root {
  --radius: 0.625rem;
  --background: oklch(1 0 0);
  --foreground: oklch(0.145 0 0);
  --card: oklch(1 0 0);
  --card-foreground: oklch(0.145 0 0);
  --popover: oklch(1 0 0);
  --popover-foreground: oklch(0.145 0 0);
